{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Encode\/timeout(_:clock:tolerance:customError:)"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timeout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"duration","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP8DurationQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"clock","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP8DurationQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"customError","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")? = nil) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncSequences","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Timeout","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Timeout","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Clock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The longest the sequence may go without an element."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"duration"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The clock that measures the gaps.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"clock"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The tolerance of the timer’s sleeps. Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"name":"tolerance"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The error to throw when the timer fires. Defaults to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"TimeoutError.timedOut(duration:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"customError"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sequence of the same elements that throws if the upstream goes quiet."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The timer starts when iteration begins and restarts with every element, so it bounds the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wait for the first element and each gap after it, never the sequence as a whole. Elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass through unchanged. When the timer fires, the upstream is cancelled and the sequence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws, without waiting for the upstream to respond to the cancellation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and elements it produces while the consumer is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"busy are buffered, so the timer measures the upstream’s gaps. A duration of zero or less","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws before the first element.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Example","anchor":"Example"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let clock = ContinuousClock()","for try await line in bytes.lines.timeout(.seconds(30), clock: clock) {","    handle(line)","}"]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customError"},{"type":"text","text":") when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duration"},{"type":"text","text":" passes between elements, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any error the upstream throws."}]}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On WASI, a sleep on a real clock (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContinuousClock"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuspendingClock"},{"text":") holds the one thread","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until its deadline, even when other work is ready, and cancelling it doesn’t end it sooner. So the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"timer can hold the thread before the upstream runs, then count that wait against it and throw even","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"though elements were ready. A test clock is unaffected.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:Sci7Afluents8SendableRzsAB7ElementRpzrlE7timeout_5clock9tolerance11customErrorAA14AsyncSequencesO7TimeoutVy_xqd__G8DurationQyd___qd__AOSgs0H0_pSgt12_Concurrency5ClockRd__lF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO6EncodeV","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"}